\fs48 \cf0 2.2.1 Hard queries\

\fs36 \
Propose two variants : one using the path relationship and one not using it but taking advantage of the quantified path pattern syntax.\
\
2.2.1 Give paths of lengths 2 or 3 from Nantes to Salt Lake City, delivered only by \'94Air France\'94,\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 MATCH p=(:Airport\{city:'Nantes'\}) -[:path*2..3]-> (:Airport\{city:'Salt Lake City'\})\
WHERE ALL(path in relationships(p) WHERE path.airline='Air France')\
RETURN p\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 2.2.2 All paths of length 2 from Paris only delivered by \'94Air France\'94 (without direct flights),\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 MATCH p=(paris:Airport\{city:'Paris'\}) -[:path*2]-> (dest:Airport)\
WHERE ALL(path in relationships(p) WHERE path.airline='Air France')  AND NOT EXISTS((paris) --> (dest))\
RETURN p\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
2.2.3 For those destinations, give per country the number of paths sorted decreasingly,\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 MATCH p=(paris:Airport\{city:'Paris'\}) -[:path*2]-> (dest:Airport)\
WHERE ALL(path in relationships(p) WHERE path.airline='Air France')  AND NOT EXISTS((paris) --> (dest))\
RETURN dest.country, COUNT(*) AS NB\
ORDER BY NB DESC\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
2.2.4 From question 2.2.2, give only those which stops at least once in the United states,\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 MATCH p=(paris:Airport\{city:'Paris'\}) -[:path*2]-> (dest:Airport)\
WHERE ALL(path in relationships(p) WHERE path.airline='Air France')  AND NOT EXISTS((paris) --> (dest))\
 AND ANY(n in nodes(p) WHERE n.country='United States')\
